.TH XARGS 1
.SH NAME
xargs \- run a command once per line of standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xargs
.I command
.RI [ arg ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Xargs
reads standard input one line at a time, tokenizes each line on
whitespace, and runs
.I command
once per line with
.I arg...
(if any were given on
.IR xargs 's
own command line) followed by that line's own tokens appended.
.PP
Unlike a POSIX xargs, which batches arguments across the whole input
up to a length limit, this is strictly one invocation of
.I command
per input line.
.I Command
is loaded as
.B .dis
(a
.B .dis
suffix is added if not already present, first from wherever it
resolves normally, then from
.BR /dis ).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/xargs.b
